From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH] io: publish the new burst state before starting processing

Capture changes burst_length and the selected mode even if no control changed.
An inactive preview can leave pipeline_changed false. In that case the process
thread keeps its initial zero burst length, consumes the frames as previews,
and never starts the JPEG postprocessor. Always publish the capture state.

--- a/src/io_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/io_pipeline.c
@@ -210,6 +210,7 @@
                 mp_flash_enable(state_io.camera);
         }
 
+        pipeline_changed = true;
         update_process_pipeline();
 
         mp_process_pipeline_capture();
